record legeos.evidence.de01-package-closure-unavailable-20260904/1 : evidence {
    title "The closure command reports honestly that no Ubuntu 26.04 index exists on this host"
    state verified
    result inconclusive
    method command
    observed_at git:9bee0dd35e5e499f688d3044c60ac13d20bac3a9
    command "cargo run -q -p xtask -- seeds closure"
    summary """
        The closure command ran and reported resolution "unavailable": this development host is Ubuntu 25.10 and carries no Ubuntu archive index at all (apt answers only from /var/lib/dpkg/status and the local LegeOS devrepo), so no package name could be resolved against Ubuntu 26.04. The declaration side is complete — 94 direct packages, fourteen exclusive provider roles all filled and none duplicated — but transitive closure, installed size, recommends and the missing list are empty because nothing was asked, not because nothing is missing.
