record legeos.evidence.nested-session-journey-20260904/1 : evidence {
    title "The nested-session journey passes end to end for the first time"
    state verified
    result pass
    method command
    observed_at git:8d74542b146fa8399817bd377094157b7bd1bb97
    summary """
        `tests/integration/nested-session.sh` reports `nested session: ok (live compositor, shell, services, CLI state journey)`: a private bus, isolated HOME/XDG, a winit compositor, the trusted-shell socket, lege-sessiond, lege-filed, lege-resourced and the portal backend all claiming their bus names, the shell surviving on the trusted socket, and the CLI round trips over app/files/settings/history/providers/resources. It had never passed: the harness waited for the shell socket under a name the compositor stopped using on 2026-09-03, and behind that lay a migration race that killed whichever daemon opened the fresh state database second. Both are fixed; the harness now also keeps its state directory when a run fails, having previously deleted the only account of why.
        """
}

record legeos.evidence.nm-tray-2-packaged-20260904/1 : evidence {
    title "nm-tray-2 is pinned, declared in the session layer, and builds as legeos-nm-tray"
    state verified
    result pass
    method command
    observed_at git:8d74542b146fa8399817bd377094157b7bd1bb97
    command "cargo run -q -p xtask -- seeds --check && cargo run -q -p xtask -- check-packaging"
    artifact "distro/forks/nm-tray-2/debian/control"
    summary """
        Both gates pass. The fork is pinned in distro/forks/manifest.toml with package = legeos-nm-tray; distro/seeds/selection.toml names it in the session layer with role network-control; the generated legeos-desktop and legeos-session-full control files both depend on it. Packaging lives at distro/forks/nm-tray-2/debian/ so the package's name, dependencies and install paths are LegeOS facts that check-packaging can see, while the source stays unvendored (ADR-0005). scripts/build-fork-deb.sh produced legeos-nm-tray 0.5.1+legeos1~g0965344 from the user's checkout: /usr/bin/nm-tray, /usr/share/applications/nm-tray.desktop (the name shell/lege-shell/src/surface/app.rs resolves when nothing declares org.legeos.NetworkTray), /etc/xdg/autostart/nm-tray-autostart.desktop, translations, Provides/Conflicts/Replaces nm-tray, and nothing under /usr/local. One thing is NOT satisfied and the build refuses rather than hides it: --popup, the session-bus forwarding slot and the X-LegeOS-* desktop keys exist only in an uncommitted working tree and are absent from every pushed commit, so a package built from the pin would install, resolve as the network provider, and do nothing when clicked. distro/forks/nm-tray-2/preflight.sh fails the build on that, and the pin cannot be trusted until those changes are pushed.
        """
}

